1
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:08,880
KUZURYU HIGH SCHOOL

2
00:00:18,380 --> 00:00:20,500
Chemistry Club

3
00:00:31,670 --> 00:00:34,830
Sweet
Tea

4
00:00:39,710 --> 00:00:41,350
Hm? From the gym?

5
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:46,310
This early in the morning?

6
00:00:51,030 --> 00:00:53,030
Oh crap! Mokichi!

7
00:00:56,330 --> 00:01:04,290
Back to the mirror, my dream getting 
farther with every step I take

8
00:01:04,290 --> 00:01:08,670
I want to come face-to-face with you

9
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:15,260
Saying to the incapable version 
of myself, "never mind"

10
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:23,170
Ahiru no Sora

11
00:01:24,750 --> 00:01:29,130
A dream slowly dismantled 
on the assembly line

12
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,420
(Suitable? Unsuitable? 
Pretty much impossible?)

13
00:01:32,570 --> 00:01:36,830
True feelings gone missing without a whisper

14
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:39,830
(Not even capable of a sigh)

15
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:46,040
None of it will end by 
placing the blame on others

16
00:01:46,210 --> 00:01:49,960
Right now, in the face of a steep slope

17
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:54,170
My heart cries out for me to "overcome it"

18
00:01:54,170 --> 00:02:01,580
Finding excuses not to try is 
something that anybody can do

19
00:02:01,790 --> 00:02:09,130
Pushing myself to run beyond, I 
went to meet a me I've never known

20
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:15,500
There's graffiti etched on the 
wall that says "never mind"

21
00:02:15,670 --> 00:02:19,610
Now, I bounce into tomorrow

22
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:29,000
A-a-are you okay?!

23
00:02:29,750 --> 00:02:31,040
Morning practice?

24
00:02:30,170 --> 00:02:34,460
The Moon and the Hoop

25
00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:33,000
Yeah, since the prelims are coming up fast.

26
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,460
Did you get hurt at all, dude?

27
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:38,920
Oh, let me introduce you.
This is Momoharu, our team captain.

28
00:02:39,130 --> 00:02:41,380
Oh... um...

29
00:02:44,750 --> 00:02:47,380
He said "Good morning, sir."

30
00:02:47,670 --> 00:02:49,880
Uh, yeah, same to you.

31
00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:52,420
So, I hear you used to shoot hoops?

32
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:54,570
Well, feel free to join us.

33
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,250
No... I didn't come here
to play with you guys or anything.

34
00:02:58,250 --> 00:02:59,080
Huh?

35
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:02,750
I just always come to school
around this time in the morning.

36
00:03:02,750 --> 00:03:04,290
What? Every day?

37
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:05,380
Yeah.

38
00:03:05,530 --> 00:03:07,580
Let him do what he wants.

39
00:03:07,580 --> 00:03:10,830
Two of our usual clowns are sleeping in,
so we're down players anyway.

40
00:03:10,830 --> 00:03:12,500
We can play 3-on-3 if he's in.

41
00:03:12,670 --> 00:03:14,500
Let's play together, Mokichi!

42
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:17,710
Since it's so early in the morning,
we can use the whole court to our heart's content!

43
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:25,430
I've already quit... playing basketball.

44
00:03:25,710 --> 00:03:27,290
Huh? But why?

45
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:28,640
You're really good at it!

46
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:30,040
No doubt about that.

47
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:33,170
The fact he can get the ball in the basket
already makes him better than Momoharu.

48
00:03:33,290 --> 00:03:34,040
Totally.

49
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:34,860
Asswipes...

50
00:03:35,130 --> 00:03:37,820
My doctor told me... that I shouldn't play.

51
00:03:37,830 --> 00:03:44,290
Kuzuryu High School Boys' Basketball Team

52
00:03:38,670 --> 00:03:42,830
I've always had a frail constitution
and I don't handle physical exercise very well.

53
00:03:43,170 --> 00:03:44,280
So that's why...

54
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:48,460
Huh? But wait, didn't you tell me
that you've played basketball since grade school?

55
00:03:48,710 --> 00:03:51,370
I did, to try and help me build some stamina.

56
00:03:51,670 --> 00:03:53,250
I'm guessing that didn't work.

57
00:03:53,250 --> 00:03:55,080
Not even in the slightest...

58
00:03:55,460 --> 00:03:58,920
I can't live up to your 
expectations. I'm sorry.

59
00:04:00,830 --> 00:04:04,330
Playing high school basketball... 
isn't a possibility for me.

60
00:04:07,130 --> 00:04:08,960
Man, what a bummer...

61
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:11,920
I was really looking forward
to shooting hoops with Mokichi.

62
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:13,730
Not everybody's fit for the court.

63
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:19,190
Actually, when we met in the gym yesterday,
Mokichi said that he was jealous of me.

64
00:04:20,330 --> 00:04:23,330
Just imagine all the practice he went through
to get good at hook shots.

65
00:04:24,290 --> 00:04:27,070
I have no doubt... he must love basketball.

66
00:04:27,710 --> 00:04:29,160
Seriously?! They're mine?!

67
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:30,710
Awesome!

68
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,370
That's okay. Because I...

69
00:04:33,710 --> 00:04:36,170
...don't need to wear them anymore.

70
00:04:37,750 --> 00:04:40,750
Loving a sport but being unable to play it...

71
00:04:41,210 --> 00:04:42,550
...I know how he feels.

72
00:04:43,670 --> 00:04:47,010
How's that? Somebody you know
have a similar problem?

73
00:04:47,330 --> 00:04:49,330
Huh? Uh, not at all!

74
00:04:49,330 --> 00:04:50,970
I was just imagining what it must be like.

75
00:04:51,250 --> 00:04:52,920
Happens all the time.

76
00:04:53,290 --> 00:04:56,960
Lots of players have to retire due to illness
or back and knee injuries.

77
00:04:57,580 --> 00:04:59,920
Loving a sport ain't 
enough to keep you in it.

78
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:06,110
Now that I think about it,
mom hasn't been sending me many replies lately.

79
00:05:07,330 --> 00:05:09,460
Does that mean she hasn't been feeling well?

80
00:05:09,830 --> 00:05:11,790
Wow. This is a surprise.

81
00:05:12,670 --> 00:05:14,880
What inspired you two to start playing shogi?

82
00:05:15,670 --> 00:05:17,330
We're betting our lunch on it.

83
00:05:17,330 --> 00:05:18,630
I already won, though.

84
00:05:18,630 --> 00:05:19,500
What the-?!

85
00:05:20,330 --> 00:05:23,380
Sorry, I didn't mean to just 
steal your seat, Nanao.

86
00:05:23,380 --> 00:05:25,260
Oh, don't worry about it. Anyways...

87
00:05:25,830 --> 00:05:28,970
I just picked this up from Mr. 
Satsuki a few minutes ago.

88
00:05:32,130 --> 00:05:35,140
The tournament bracket is out!

89
00:05:35,140 --> 00:05:40,080
Prelims! Prelims! Prelims!

90
00:05:36,630 --> 00:05:37,850
Shut up!

91
00:05:38,290 --> 00:05:40,080
Our first opponent will be...

92
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:42,040
Shinmaruko
Shinjotowa
Kuzuryu

93
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:43,500
Shinmaruko
Shinjotowa
Kuzuryu

94
00:05:43,830 --> 00:05:46,880
Maru High is in the same block that we are...

95
00:05:47,450 --> 00:05:49,630
Wh-wh-what about Kitasumi?!

96
00:05:50,210 --> 00:05:52,040
Yes! They're in another block!

97
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:53,880
We're safe from dealing with 
any of them for a while then!

98
00:05:54,330 --> 00:05:56,420
You can't avoid the inevitable, guys.

99
00:05:56,750 --> 00:05:59,210
What kind of team are we 
facing in the first round?

100
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:00,880
Don't you have data on them or something?

101
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:07,000
Uh, well, Shinjotowa is a team that...
has 3 players in the 190 cm range.

102
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,380
I know that one of them is 196 cm tall.

103
00:06:09,670 --> 00:06:13,210
The average height of
their sophomore players is 184 cm.

104
00:06:13,210 --> 00:06:15,540
So, we're dealing with a team of giants.

105
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:18,540
Too many kids going through
ridiculous growth spurts these days.

106
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:19,770
You're one to talk.

107
00:06:21,730 --> 00:06:24,210
All right. Let's get to practicing!

108
00:06:24,210 --> 00:06:26,500
Hold up. I don't see Kite anywhere.

109
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:29,080
Kite's busy right now.
He got stuck with extra lessons today.

110
00:06:29,070 --> 00:06:31,540
Hah! Guess he's an idiot 
outside of basketball.

111
00:06:31,830 --> 00:06:36,460
You guys should consider following his example.
Mid-terms are next week, you know?

112
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:38,500
Are you serious?!

113
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:48,080
Hey, Chucky! You're defending too high!

114
00:06:48,540 --> 00:06:50,040
Pay more attention to the 
distance you're leaving!

115
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:51,830
Hiyah!

116
00:06:52,210 --> 00:06:54,580
Yasuhara, that's your 7th foul today!

117
00:06:54,790 --> 00:06:56,460
Drop and give me 20 more push-ups right now!

118
00:06:58,210 --> 00:06:59,790
Next! 2-on-2!

119
00:06:59,790 --> 00:07:00,960
Rotate positions!

120
00:07:03,230 --> 00:07:05,710
There's pretty much no time 
left before the prelims.

121
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,460
What do you think, do we stand a shot?

122
00:07:07,790 --> 00:07:10,750
To be perfectly frank, it 
will be an uphill battle.

123
00:07:10,750 --> 00:07:12,910
Right... you really cut to the point.

124
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:16,420
I think the biggest obstacle at this point
is our lack of height.

125
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:20,210
We only have 3 players on the team
who come in at over 180 centimeters.

126
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:24,130
We were able to go up against Kitasumi
on pretty even terms in that regard,

127
00:07:24,790 --> 00:07:28,170
but the only reason that worked out
is because Kitasumi is on the short side overall.

128
00:07:28,960 --> 00:07:31,790
Our first match in the prelims
is going to be completely different.

129
00:07:32,250 --> 00:07:33,880
Especially under the basket.

130
00:07:34,330 --> 00:07:38,310
If that's the case, then we really need somebody with height,

131
00:07:38,310 --> 00:07:40,270
even if it's not that Mokichi guy.

132
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:42,250
You're right.

133
00:07:45,380 --> 00:07:48,630
Well, we shouldn't waste time
worrying about what we don't have.

134
00:07:48,630 --> 00:07:51,290
So let's work hard to overcome
any challenges on our own.

135
00:07:51,750 --> 00:07:54,210
Considering how high you can jump, it's pretty much

136
00:07:54,210 --> 00:07:56,210
like having two players for the price of one.

137
00:07:56,210 --> 00:07:56,880
Trust me.

138
00:07:57,330 --> 00:07:58,580
Oh-ho?

139
00:07:58,580 --> 00:08:00,330
That's some high praise coming from you.

140
00:08:00,540 --> 00:08:03,510
But your lack of scoring ability practically
puts us down a player,

141
00:08:03,510 --> 00:08:05,000
so we come out even in the end.

142
00:08:05,330 --> 00:08:06,460
Ouch...

143
00:08:07,420 --> 00:08:12,170
Extra Lessons

144
00:08:09,460 --> 00:08:11,170
You have a good head on your shoulders.

145
00:08:11,170 --> 00:08:12,170
'Course, I do.

146
00:08:12,670 --> 00:08:13,540
Listen up.

147
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:16,920
You were suspended for two weeks
immediately after school started.

148
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:21,100
If you don't put some effort into studying,
you'll get left behind quickly.

149
00:08:21,670 --> 00:08:26,060
And don't forget... I'm holding you
to your promise of not getting into any fights.

150
00:08:26,580 --> 00:08:27,920
I haven't forgotten.

151
00:08:28,420 --> 00:08:31,830
The prelims are about to start,
I'm not gonna throw it all away for a fight.

152
00:08:36,130 --> 00:08:37,540
A'ight, time to head for the gy-

153
00:08:37,540 --> 00:08:38,500
Wow!

154
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:39,670
I didn't know that!

155
00:08:39,660 --> 00:08:43,330
Take this and then put it over 
in this one, and it's done.

156
00:08:44,750 --> 00:08:45,830
It's the beanstalk...

157
00:08:47,380 --> 00:08:49,330
Incredible! You really did it!

158
00:08:49,330 --> 00:08:51,420
You've got a real knack for this, Mokichi!

159
00:08:51,420 --> 00:08:54,080
Most definitely, everybody around here
considers you the ace of the chem club!

160
00:08:54,420 --> 00:08:55,550
"Ace"?

161
00:08:56,290 --> 00:08:58,510
Can a chemistry club even have an "ace"...?

162
00:08:58,670 --> 00:09:00,500
This reminds me, Mokichi.

163
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:03,580
I hear that you turned down
the basketball team on their offer yesterday.

164
00:09:03,580 --> 00:09:05,170
I was really surprised.

165
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:07,630
I had no idea that your physical condition
was bad enough

166
00:09:07,630 --> 00:09:08,980
that the doctor made you stop playing...

167
00:09:09,460 --> 00:09:11,290
Oh, but hey, you're safe with us!

168
00:09:11,750 --> 00:09:14,190
We'll never make you do anything
too strenuous around here, Mokichi.

169
00:09:14,750 --> 00:09:15,670
That was a lie.

170
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:16,630
Huh?

171
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:20,420
I lied. About the doctor.

172
00:09:22,460 --> 00:09:25,210
You lied? But why would you do that?

173
00:09:27,210 --> 00:09:31,170
Because teams always quit trying to recruit me
after I tell them that.

174
00:09:32,420 --> 00:09:33,460
Quit trying?

175
00:09:35,460 --> 00:09:39,140
Well isn't that an interesting story?
Start 'splaining it to me.

176
00:09:40,850 --> 00:09:43,130
Wh-who are you and why are you here?

177
00:09:43,130 --> 00:09:45,540
I'm just here to chat with the beanstalk.

178
00:09:46,130 --> 00:09:47,580
Why the hell would you lie to us?

179
00:09:48,130 --> 00:09:51,540
If you didn't want to play,
then you could've just told us that straight up.

180
00:09:51,710 --> 00:09:54,490
It's really... none of your business.

181
00:09:58,290 --> 00:10:00,170
You're right about that.

182
00:10:00,170 --> 00:10:02,830
I don't give a single shit 
about you or your problems.

183
00:10:03,420 --> 00:10:07,540
But some of us believed in you
and really took that lie to heart, jackass!

184
00:10:09,750 --> 00:10:11,460
What's going on?! What was that noise?!

185
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:14,000
S-Sir! Please do something about him!

186
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:16,260
Oh shit, this is bad...

187
00:10:16,540 --> 00:10:18,790
Ugh! What is that smell?!

188
00:10:18,790 --> 00:10:20,290
I'm very sorry.

189
00:10:20,290 --> 00:10:23,720
I was clumsy and accidentally
spilt ammonia solution on him.

190
00:10:26,960 --> 00:10:28,290
Please forgive me.

191
00:10:28,290 --> 00:10:30,500
Forget it. No big deal.

192
00:10:31,170 --> 00:10:32,170
Dammit.

193
00:10:32,170 --> 00:10:35,380
Why the hell am I getting all bent out of shape
on behalf of the shrimp?

194
00:10:39,540 --> 00:10:40,880
Sorry to bother you, Nanao.

195
00:10:41,130 --> 00:10:43,580
Can you pass them to me from further away?

196
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:45,080
Sure. I can do that.

197
00:10:47,210 --> 00:10:49,290
Kurumatani is different today.

198
00:10:49,580 --> 00:10:51,540
He's incredibly focused...

199
00:10:53,750 --> 00:10:55,670
...don't need to wear them anymore.

200
00:10:55,670 --> 00:10:58,670
My doctor told me... that I shouldn't play.

201
00:11:08,930 --> 00:11:12,170
Hard to believe he can sink 
threes like that at his height.

202
00:11:12,420 --> 00:11:14,650
His skills are really... impressive.

203
00:11:17,130 --> 00:11:19,040
Whoa, check him out.

204
00:11:19,040 --> 00:11:21,000
He's gotta be at least 2 meters tall, yeah?

205
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,830
Wish we had somebody like him
on our school's volleyball team.

206
00:11:24,130 --> 00:11:26,080
What am I, chopped liver?

207
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:28,620
Must be nice to reap all 
the benefits of being tall.

208
00:11:30,540 --> 00:11:32,040
So annoying...

209
00:11:32,250 --> 00:11:35,460
Huh? Hey, asshole! What did you just say?!

210
00:11:35,880 --> 00:11:37,760
He's, like, kind of creepy.

211
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,380
You want me to kick your 
ass to the curb, punk?

212
00:11:40,380 --> 00:11:41,720
Uh, no, I...

213
00:11:46,790 --> 00:11:47,670
Not again...!

214
00:11:47,670 --> 00:11:49,670
C'mon, shithead. Answer my damn question.

215
00:11:49,670 --> 00:11:51,500
Ew, gross. What's his problem?

216
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:53,900
Enough bullshit, hurry up and say something!

217
00:11:54,130 --> 00:11:56,710
Ugh, just forget this loser 
and let's get out of here.

218
00:11:56,710 --> 00:11:58,130
Freaks like this make me wanna puke.

219
00:11:58,540 --> 00:12:00,080
Could say the same about you.

220
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:01,580
Total barf bags!

221
00:12:02,330 --> 00:12:03,280
Huh...?

222
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:06,420
Sweet, that was worth the trip.

223
00:12:06,420 --> 00:12:08,210
I thought for sure her 
panties would be black.

224
00:12:08,210 --> 00:12:10,250
Yo! What the hell are you doing to my woman?!

225
00:12:10,250 --> 00:12:13,210
Who the hell decided that she was YOUR woman?

226
00:12:13,580 --> 00:12:15,880
Wh-who do you think...?

227
00:12:17,290 --> 00:12:19,170
See? I told you we shouldn't bother.

228
00:12:19,170 --> 00:12:22,500
Guys like us just aren't cut 
out for this hero stuff.

229
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:24,890
We got a peek at some panties, 
so I consider it a win.

230
00:12:25,080 --> 00:12:28,040
Man, I missed tonight's 
"Kumagoro Animal Nation"...

231
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:30,250
Please turn... right...

232
00:12:30,790 --> 00:12:33,960
Dude, you better not just 
be faking it. I'll drop you!

233
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:37,710
This is my house...

234
00:12:39,820 --> 00:12:43,420
Hot damn, are you one of those 
super rich kids or what?

235
00:12:44,130 --> 00:12:47,880
I could smell piles of cash
coming from this guy a mile away.

236
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:48,380
Good evening.

237
00:12:48,380 --> 00:12:49,240
For real?!

238
00:12:49,240 --> 00:12:51,710
Let's claim a little 
reward. For our good deed.

239
00:12:54,710 --> 00:12:57,170
Holy shit! A private court?!

240
00:12:57,420 --> 00:12:59,420
We're still in Japan, right?

241
00:13:00,420 --> 00:13:02,880
Dudes, let's try out our 
footwork on this thing!

242
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:04,880
We just finished doing all that at practice!

243
00:13:04,880 --> 00:13:07,130
No way, this can't be real.

244
00:13:07,330 --> 00:13:09,350
Just how much money does his family have?!

245
00:13:10,130 --> 00:13:10,960
Who's there?!

246
00:13:13,420 --> 00:13:16,500
Oh my, are all you boys from Kaname's school?

247
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:18,900
Yes, ma'am! We're his good friends!

248
00:13:19,750 --> 00:13:21,400
Oh no! He collapsed at school again?!

249
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:25,130
Yes. And we're the ones
who made sure he got home safely!

250
00:13:25,460 --> 00:13:28,570
Dear madam, allow me to offer my assistance.

251
00:13:28,750 --> 00:13:30,580
You cheat! I'm the one who carried him all t-

252
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:31,580
No, it was me who did!

253
00:13:31,580 --> 00:13:32,210
Quit lying!

254
00:13:32,210 --> 00:13:33,210
You're the liar!

255
00:13:32,670 --> 00:13:34,040
Th-thank you, boys...

256
00:13:33,210 --> 00:13:34,040
You!

257
00:13:34,040 --> 00:13:36,540
Excuse my bluntness, but 
may I have your name?

258
00:13:36,540 --> 00:13:38,960
I'm Kaname's older sister, my name is Sayuri.

259
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:40,040
A beautiful name.

260
00:13:43,130 --> 00:13:47,250
Um, so is this court like... 
part of your house?

261
00:13:47,670 --> 00:13:48,680
That's right.

262
00:13:48,680 --> 00:13:51,250
Kaname was still just an elementary student.

263
00:13:51,250 --> 00:13:54,310
It was an outrageous request, but our father did it for him.

264
00:13:54,790 --> 00:13:58,020
How is a private basketball court "outrageous"
instead of just plain "impossible"...?

265
00:13:58,380 --> 00:14:03,670
After that, he would play around out there every day,
from morning until night.

266
00:14:03,670 --> 00:14:04,740
Wow.

267
00:14:04,740 --> 00:14:06,170
And in middle school,

268
00:14:06,170 --> 00:14:08,980
he went to this place
called Saijo known for their tough basketball team.

269
00:14:09,630 --> 00:14:12,200
Seriously?! This guy went to Saijo?!

270
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:15,790
Even in 6th grade, he was already
upwards of 180 centimeters tall.

271
00:14:13,500 --> 00:14:15,790
So delicious! Delectable!

272
00:14:16,250 --> 00:14:18,420
So in middle school, he was 
made a starter right away.

273
00:14:19,170 --> 00:14:23,380
He was a shining star, with the hopes
of the team and school riding on him.

274
00:14:23,830 --> 00:14:24,670
I also thought...

275
00:14:24,670 --> 00:14:25,830
Stop it!

276
00:14:27,080 --> 00:14:28,130
Kaname!

277
00:14:29,420 --> 00:14:32,250
Hearing that stuff... really aggravates me.

278
00:14:33,460 --> 00:14:35,630
Nobody gave any thought to how I felt,

279
00:14:35,630 --> 00:14:37,730
nor how hard it was to deal with everyone's expectations.

280
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:42,190
All I ever wanted to do... was 
just play some basketball.

281
00:14:42,210 --> 00:14:44,170
Seijo
Miyasakae

282
00:14:42,750 --> 00:14:43,880
And yet...!

283
00:14:44,150 --> 00:14:46,210
He can't run worth a shit.

284
00:14:46,460 --> 00:14:47,920
All he's got is height.

285
00:14:48,650 --> 00:14:53,630
People kept expecting so much of me
and then were disappointed all on their own!

286
00:14:54,170 --> 00:14:55,330
Kaname...

287
00:14:56,710 --> 00:14:58,040
That sounds pretty nice, man.

288
00:15:00,630 --> 00:15:03,960
Nobody even bothers...
to expect anything from guys like us.

289
00:15:07,290 --> 00:15:08,830
That's for damn sure.

290
00:15:09,380 --> 00:15:11,890
We're basically just a 
pimple on society's ass.

291
00:15:12,170 --> 00:15:15,670
But that doesn't stop us from 
trying to win the inter-high.

292
00:15:15,670 --> 00:15:16,850
It's almost funny, eh?

293
00:15:17,330 --> 00:15:18,810
The inter-high...

294
00:15:19,040 --> 00:15:20,830
Yo, let us get in on some of the fun.

295
00:15:19,790 --> 00:15:21,420
What do they mean by that?

296
00:15:20,830 --> 00:15:21,420
Sure.

297
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:23,000
You wanna put 5,000 funbucks down on this?

298
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:24,000
I thought that Kuzu High
didn't have a boys' basketball team.

299
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,500
Bring it. I'll bet all the funbucks you want.

300
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:26,290
I thought that's why you applied there.

301
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:26,290
Don't underestimate the 
power of funbucks, Momoharu.

302
00:15:26,290 --> 00:15:28,540
To give up on ever playing basketball again.

303
00:15:29,750 --> 00:15:31,540
Yeah, but...

304
00:15:34,450 --> 00:15:37,710
...it turns out there 
is... a basketball team.

305
00:15:38,950 --> 00:15:40,910
BOYS'
BASKETBALL
TEAM

306
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:40,920
He lied?

307
00:15:41,130 --> 00:15:43,420
All that stuff about the doctor was BS.

308
00:15:43,420 --> 00:15:45,380
That stupid beanstalk really pisses me off.

309
00:15:45,750 --> 00:15:48,090
Why would he even bother 
to lie to us like that?

310
00:15:48,290 --> 00:15:50,750
Cuz he's a 2-meter-tall freshman.

311
00:15:50,750 --> 00:15:52,750
Any high school would kill to have him.

312
00:15:52,750 --> 00:15:55,580
Just putting him on a team
would help motivate the other members.

313
00:15:55,960 --> 00:16:00,520
With a ton of expectations piled up like that,
anybody would snap from the pressure.

314
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:02,500
Just like that.

315
00:16:07,480 --> 00:16:09,960
It doesn't matter whether he's sick or not.

316
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:12,450
If he's not interested in joining,
then there's nothing we can do.

317
00:16:12,670 --> 00:16:13,830
Hey, Kite.

318
00:16:13,830 --> 00:16:15,790
Did Mokichi really say all that stuff?

319
00:16:15,960 --> 00:16:18,130
Why the hell would I lie 
to you about what he said?

320
00:16:18,130 --> 00:16:19,920
C'mon dude, just forget that beanstalk.

321
00:16:23,130 --> 00:16:26,420
Only 4 seconds left... only 
one chance left to score!

322
00:16:29,500 --> 00:16:30,420
I gotta block!

323
00:16:36,510 --> 00:16:37,130
Yeah!

324
00:16:37,130 --> 00:16:38,540
We did it!

325
00:16:54,630 --> 00:16:56,000
Just a dream...?

326
00:16:57,210 --> 00:17:01,170
Oh yeah... I took the day 
off from school today...

327
00:17:04,710 --> 00:17:08,040
Nobody even bothers...
to expect anything from guys like us.

328
00:17:08,210 --> 00:17:11,460
But that doesn't stop us from 
trying to win the inter-high.

329
00:17:11,750 --> 00:17:13,040
It's almost funny, eh?

330
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,500
I wonder... are they serious...?

331
00:17:19,580 --> 00:17:20,930
Welcome.

332
00:17:21,330 --> 00:17:25,170
Basketball shoes these days... 
seem kind of futuristic.

333
00:17:25,750 --> 00:17:27,710
I can get your size, if 
you'd like to try them on.

334
00:17:27,710 --> 00:17:29,250
I bet you must be about a 30?

335
00:17:29,380 --> 00:17:31,000
Uh, no thanks.

336
00:17:31,610 --> 00:17:33,170
I'm just looking.

337
00:17:33,500 --> 00:17:35,420
I don't play basketball anymore.

338
00:17:35,750 --> 00:17:39,670
Oh, is that so? That's a 
shame, since you're so tall.

339
00:17:40,960 --> 00:17:42,250
Sorry to bother you.

340
00:17:42,710 --> 00:17:45,500
Ah! These ones! These are 
the shoes our Senpai has!

341
00:17:46,580 --> 00:17:47,960
Is that you, Shigeyoshi?

342
00:17:50,380 --> 00:17:52,830
Tsu-Tsukishima?!

343
00:17:52,840 --> 00:17:55,000
Wow! It's been, like, forever!

344
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,130
I'm so surprised to see you!
What are you doing out here?

345
00:17:58,330 --> 00:18:00,290
Who's this? An old classmate of yours, Kyoko?

346
00:18:00,290 --> 00:18:02,500
That's right! From back in middle school!

347
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:03,880
C'mon, say hello!

348
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:05,250
Uh, my name is Kanam-

349
00:18:05,250 --> 00:18:06,630
Speak up!

350
00:18:07,250 --> 00:18:10,750
You haven't changed. Your eyebrows
are as thick as ever, Senpai.

351
00:18:10,750 --> 00:18:11,830
Shut it!

352
00:18:13,040 --> 00:18:15,880
Are you sure, about leaving 
your friend behind?

353
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:17,500
Oh, she's fine, don't worry.

354
00:18:17,790 --> 00:18:19,660
I've got other plans today, anyways.

355
00:18:19,880 --> 00:18:23,330
But hey, I wanna know!
You were looking at basketball shoes earlier, right?

356
00:18:23,630 --> 00:18:25,880
Does this mean that you 
started playing again?!

357
00:18:26,080 --> 00:18:29,880
No, uh, it's just a habit that I've had
ever since I was young...

358
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:32,130
...hanging out in shoe stores like that
helps calm me down.

359
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:33,790
Boo!

360
00:18:33,960 --> 00:18:35,800
Don't get my hopes up like that!

361
00:18:36,040 --> 00:18:38,000
I had such big expectations for you.

362
00:18:38,290 --> 00:18:40,130
Now I'm just super disappointed.

363
00:18:42,580 --> 00:18:44,750
So I'm curious, do you remember?

364
00:18:44,750 --> 00:18:46,460
Our summer vacation in 2nd year?

365
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:49,700
There was this big rumor that spread through the whole

366
00:18:49,700 --> 00:18:52,940
girls' team about how you had a huge crush on me.

367
00:18:53,130 --> 00:18:56,710
Th-th-th-th-th-that was just gossip, I swear.

368
00:18:56,710 --> 00:18:58,500
Huh? So you didn't?!

369
00:18:58,830 --> 00:19:01,710
Th... That's right...

370
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:06,420
Darn, that's too bad.

371
00:19:11,880 --> 00:19:13,000
Then... how about right now?

372
00:19:14,130 --> 00:19:14,960
Huh?

373
00:19:15,210 --> 00:19:17,690
Uh, no, actually, well... honestly,

374
00:19:17,690 --> 00:19:20,930
I don't feel any different about you now as I did back then.

375
00:19:20,930 --> 00:19:23,290
That's totally not what 
I was asking you about!

376
00:19:25,170 --> 00:19:26,220
I meant sports!

377
00:19:26,790 --> 00:19:28,750
Are you playing on any other teams right now?

378
00:19:29,710 --> 00:19:32,420
Uhhh... well... the chemistry club.

379
00:19:35,710 --> 00:19:37,170
Is that fun for you?

380
00:19:38,210 --> 00:19:41,630
Yes. It's something... I enjoy.

381
00:19:42,540 --> 00:19:43,790
Oh?

382
00:19:45,580 --> 00:19:46,750
More than basketball?

383
00:19:59,920 --> 00:20:02,670
It's fun... even more than basketball.

384
00:20:03,420 --> 00:20:04,390
I see.

385
00:20:05,330 --> 00:20:06,850
Then I'm happy for you!

386
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:16,380
No... actually...!

387
00:20:16,380 --> 00:20:17,290
Kyoko!

388
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:20,740
What're you doing? The library's gonna close.

389
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:22,860
Oh shoot! I totally spaced!

390
00:20:22,860 --> 00:20:23,960
Gotta study for the test!

391
00:20:23,960 --> 00:20:26,170
Give me a break already, jeez.

392
00:20:26,170 --> 00:20:28,410
You're the one who asked 
me to help you study.

393
00:20:29,080 --> 00:20:30,960
You remember him, right, Shigeyoshi?

394
00:20:30,960 --> 00:20:32,880
This is Fujita, another 
senior from middle school.

395
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:34,380
Uh, nice to see you.

396
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:37,340
Actually, we've been dating 
each other recently.

397
00:20:40,130 --> 00:20:41,580
See you later, Shigeyoshi!

398
00:20:41,580 --> 00:20:42,760
Uh, sure.

399
00:20:45,290 --> 00:20:46,250
Who was that?

400
00:20:46,250 --> 00:20:48,960
He was a freshman
at our school, remember? Shigeyoshi!

401
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:52,170
Oh, right. You mean Mokichi, the one who...

402
00:20:52,170 --> 00:20:54,040
That's not his name!

403
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:03,170
Kaname?

404
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:07,460
He's 180 cm tall, dude!

405
00:21:07,670 --> 00:21:08,790
That's nuts!

406
00:21:10,580 --> 00:21:13,750
The size of the court and length of games
is a step up from junior basketball.

407
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:15,630
You'll get used to it.

408
00:21:15,630 --> 00:21:17,580
Just work on building up your stamina, man.

409
00:21:21,420 --> 00:21:23,540
Dammit, right when we needed him!

410
00:21:23,540 --> 00:21:24,750
Don't be like that.

411
00:21:24,750 --> 00:21:26,720
It's what we get for relying on a freshman.

412
00:21:28,430 --> 00:21:29,670
Again, really?

413
00:21:29,670 --> 00:21:31,460
It's fine. Just go home today.

414
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,630
He hasn't improved at all this year, I swear.

415
00:21:35,040 --> 00:21:38,360
Doesn't he understand that he's
on the verge of being left behind?

416
00:21:46,670 --> 00:21:49,670
I am... such an idiot.

417
00:21:50,460 --> 00:21:55,000
The one person who I disappointed
the most... was myself.

418
00:21:56,210 --> 00:22:00,290
I've gotta get back there... one more time.
No matter what!

419
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:17,960
Even if things aren't going well on my own

420
00:22:18,500 --> 00:22:22,170
There's a simple way to turn it all around

421
00:22:24,080 --> 00:22:29,130
A light falls down on an 
exit previously unseen

422
00:22:29,580 --> 00:22:33,290
That's where the path to tomorrow lies

423
00:22:34,080 --> 00:22:40,000
I was never really alone to begin with

424
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:45,170
You were in the scenery reflected in my eyes

425
00:22:45,330 --> 00:22:51,670
I can go anywhere so long as you stay there

426
00:22:51,670 --> 00:22:56,540
There are no such things as limits

427
00:22:56,540 --> 00:23:01,710
Just having you by my side makes me stronger

428
00:23:01,920 --> 00:23:08,790
We'll pick ourselves up as 
often as needed and keep moving

429
00:23:08,920 --> 00:23:16,630
Oh oh oh, oh oh oh, oh oh oh,

430
00:23:16,630 --> 00:23:19,790
Until the very last second

431
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,630
Don't give up and keep fighting

432
00:23:22,630 --> 00:23:29,710
A shining light is undoubtedly 
waiting for us down this path

433
00:23:30,970 --> 00:23:35,390
Ahiru no Sora
Next Time: Light

434
00:23:31,710 --> 00:23:34,040
Next time: "Light."

